TA-rapl
====

Collects power telemetry from /sys/class/powercap (RAPL energy counters in microjoules, package/core domain limits) and, as a fallback, from hwmon power sensors (/sys/class/hwmon power*_input). Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype rapl:status) and rapl.* metrics (energy counters, current watts, counts) to index=metrics (sourcetype rapl:metrics), with dashboards.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * none - pure /sys reads (powercap when present, hwmon otherwise)
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="rapl:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="rapl:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="rapl.*" by host
  | mstats avg("rapl.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=rapl:status  (powercap domains, energy_uj, hwmon power chips)
Metrics: rapl.<domain>_energy_uj, rapl.<chip>_<key>_watts, rapl.powercap_count
Dashboards: TA-Rapl > Rapl Overview / Rapl Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-rapl/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * Intel RAPL (/sys/class/powercap/intel-rapl*) only; AMD hosts fall back to hwmon power chips.
  * energy_uj counters are cumulative - take rate() in search-time math.

License
-------
SOURCE-AVAILABLE (see LICENSE) - free personal, educational and evaluation
use; commercial or production use requires a paid license from BentleyPC
LLC (https://www.bentleypc.com/TA-rapl).

Enter your key (format BP-...) after purchase using EITHER method:

  1. Splunk Web: open the app, click "License" in the nav, click a row to
     open the key entry page, paste the key and Save.

  2. File (headless / forwarder friendly): create the file
     $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-rapl/local/license.conf with:

         [settings]
         telemetry_enabled = 1
         key = BP-xxxxxxxxxxxx

     No restart required - the hourly beacon reads this file on every run.

Set telemetry_enabled = 0 to keep the key for validation but pause all
outbound beacons. The beacon sends only: license key, hostname, app name
and app version to the BentleyPC license API (see api_base in
default/license.conf). It is telemetry only - never a license check that
blocks functionality.
